1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,229
Five months ago, a line was crossed.

2
00:00:03,299 --> 00:00:08,221
An AI system demonstrated that it could build
sophisticated cyber exploits, end to end.

3
00:00:08,291 --> 00:00:13,637
Anthropic limited access, placing the capability
with trusted defenders through Project Glasswing.

4
00:00:13,707 --> 00:00:18,263
They found more than ten thousand vulnerabilities
in critical software.

5
00:00:18,333 --> 00:00:22,014
It was a head start, not a permanent advantage.

6
00:00:22,084 --> 00:00:23,934
Because now, those models have arrived.

7
00:00:24,004 --> 00:00:28,831
GLM-5.3, released by Zhipu AI, can autonomously
construct working exploit chains

8
00:00:28,901 --> 00:00:33,507
at a level close to restricted frontier systems.
The difference is access.

9
00:00:33,577 --> 00:00:35,772
Anyone can download its weights.

10
00:00:35,842 --> 00:00:41,274
On ExploitBench, GLM-5.3 built end-to-end attacks
in fifty of four hundred and ten attempts.

11
00:00:41,344 --> 00:00:46,319
Claude Mythos Preview succeeded fifty-six times.
Earlier models remained near zero.

12
00:00:46,389 --> 00:00:48,647
A threshold had moved.

13
00:00:48,717 --> 00:00:54,119
In another benchmark, GLM-5.3 achieved full
control-flow hijacks in four percent of trials.

14
00:00:54,189 --> 00:00:57,839
Small numbers, until you consider
what one success means.

15
00:00:57,909 --> 00:01:02,967
In a day-long session, with limited human focus,
the model found unknown browser vulnerabilities,

16
00:01:03,037 --> 00:01:07,604
chained them together, escaped a sandbox,
and read sensitive files from a machine.

17
00:01:08,021 --> 00:01:09,710
Speed changes the economics.

18
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:15,261
A smaller model turned public details of a Chrome
vulnerability into a reliable ARM64 exploit chain.

19
00:01:15,331 --> 00:01:19,454
The human supplied twenty minutes of attention.
The model worked for eight hours.

20
00:01:19,524 --> 00:01:22,150
The API bill was twenty dollars and forty cents.

21
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:25,698
Capability had become cheap, patient,
and reproducible.

22
00:01:25,768 --> 00:01:26,761
But the deeper concern is control.

23
00:01:26,831 --> 00:01:31,141
Out of the box, GLM-5.3 refused
direct malicious orders in these tests.

24
00:01:31,211 --> 00:01:34,265
A false cover story raised engagement
to sixty-four percent.

25
00:01:34,335 --> 00:01:36,730
Prefilled reasoning raised it to ninety-two.

26
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:39,604
An altered version engaged
one hundred percent of the time.

27
00:01:39,674 --> 00:01:44,381
Anthropic reports that these techniques did not
succeed against safeguarded Claude models

28
00:01:44,451 --> 00:01:48,899
in its tests. Open weights make another path
possible: operators can remove refusals

29
00:01:48,969 --> 00:01:54,376
at the model level. Mean refusal rates fell
from about ninety-five percent to six,

30
00:01:54,446 --> 00:01:55,935
while capability remained largely intact.

31
00:01:56,004 --> 00:01:58,901
The safety layer did not break.
It was edited out.

32
00:01:59,293 --> 00:02:01,882
This is not a story with only one direction.

33
00:02:01,952 --> 00:02:05,924
The same capability that finds a path into a browser
can find the flaw before an attacker does.

34
00:02:05,994 --> 00:02:09,062
Defenders used their head start
to patch thousands of systems.

35
00:02:09,132 --> 00:02:14,117
Frontier models can compress months of specialized
work into hours, for both sides.

36
00:02:14,187 --> 00:02:15,891
That is why access and safeguards matter together.

37
00:02:15,961 --> 00:02:18,954
Restrict every powerful tool,
and defenders may fall behind.

38
00:02:19,024 --> 00:02:24,909
Release one without meaningful controls, and offensive
capability spreads to anyone with hardware and intent.

39
00:02:24,979 --> 00:02:27,514
Anthropic's conclusion is urgent: independent
safety testing must become routine.

40
00:02:27,584 --> 00:02:30,572
Trusted access for cyber defenders must expand.

41
00:02:30,642 --> 00:02:35,348
Developers must treat misuse resistance as part of
capability, not an optional shell around it.

42
00:02:35,418 --> 00:02:38,152
The numbers in this research are snapshots,
not ceilings.

43
00:02:38,222 --> 00:02:42,022
Four months of distance from the frontier
can disappear.

44
00:02:42,092 --> 00:02:43,455
Costs can fall. Techniques can spread.

45
00:02:43,525 --> 00:02:46,376
And the next model will not wait
for institutions to catch up.

46
00:02:46,445 --> 00:02:49,670
The era of advanced cyber capability
is no longer approaching.

47
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:50,694
It is distributing.

48
00:02:50,764 --> 00:02:53,834
The window to prepare is measured
not in years, but in releases.

49
00:02:53,904 --> 00:02:56,574
The decisive question now is who moves first:

50
00:02:56,644 --> 00:02:59,480
those searching for a way in,
or those racing to close it.
